Provide a brief outline of topics to be covered - this description will be displayed in ACM's Digital Library.

The ACM International Conference on Quantum Computing and Systems is the primary ACM venue on quantum systems with a focus on architecture, systems, programming languages and compilers, design automation for quantum computing.
 
Who is your anticipated audience?

Academia, industry and reseachers from labs in quantum computing.
 
How will papers be solicited?
        
Web site, CFP flyers at venues and mailing lists

How will papers be selected?
        
Double blind review process

